      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5babfb12bf9da87d36048640|full_name}: well, by this logic everyone should have a green icon for their avatars by now lol\nI mean, you're not wrong, if people want they can find a way to make it seems like it has good performance, but how many will actually do that just because people are using a filter that hide their avatars?\nProbably only trolls and crashers, but I don't think there are so many to make this function useless. And just to be clear, this request was made without taking into account trolls or crashers, because I know very well it will be useless for them, in the end, even if you try to stop them they still find the way to be annoying by using other methods. \nI'm talking about normal people, and this function is only a simplification of the current system, because even now I can block avatars with bad performance, but I have to do it manually",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-31T22:05:58.611Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The current safety system in my opinion is very effective, but I think it makes more sense if there is the possibility of blocking the heaviest avatars instead of blocking an entire range of users just because of their rank. Very often the range of users that are blocked are from visitors to users (or at least I often do so) but often the problem is 2 or 3 avatars that use a lot of resources. And yes, it is possible to block individual avatars, but often it's not easy when maybe the world is big or there are too many people, so it becomes difficult to identify, select users and block their avatars.\nSo I think it would be useful to have settings to block avatars with bad performance, maybe being able to choose between red and yellow ones, even better if you can choose what to block those avatars like in the current safety system, obviously all of this excluding friends",
